for honor was first announced in 2015  and is scheduled to be released in 2017.  we recently got our grubby hands on the  alpha version and have unearthed  seven reasons to be excited about for  honor  first a quick note to my mum mother it  is not a spelling mistake  honor is spelt without a u literally  everywhere except england right now  that's cleared up on with the gameplay  remember being a kid and arguing about  who would win a fight between that guy  from onimusha one of the lost vikings  and sir lancelot  well now you can see first hand knights  vikings and my personal favorite samurai  meet head to head to head and as you  would expect it's bloody as hell  the demeanor the weapon choice the skill  set the aesthetic of each character is  unique to each class  meaning when you wield a sword as a  samurai it looks the part and you feel  damn important and speaking of blood  executions executions  executions you will have the opportunity  to slay your enemies with a brutal final  blow  preventing them from being healed by  another teammate there are some mesmeric  final impacts  but the greatest of all is from the  samurai who are more than happy to  behead anyone that stands in front of  them  get up from that darling if you're the  one receiving the blade to the back of  the head then use the countdown timer  well  by switching to tactical view and  checking where you should next attack on  the battlefield  in real time you can view any area of  the fight and find out which one of your  team requires support or maybe spot a  hull in the opposition's defense  let's look at the fighting mechanics as  they shake up the typical one button  defense used by assassin's creed or the  arkham series  in for honor you are given visual cues  to help determine where to defend  you can block in three ways left right  or forward  when you are blocking left your  character moves into that position which  allows you to predict the attack  patterns of your enemy  but worse still they can predict yours  but you also need to be careful because  it's possible to fake an attack  too if you are absolutely getting  pummeled on the battlefield  you can adopt a more defensive approach  which could give your teammates chance  to get to your position  that might sound a little boring but by  waiting an extra five seconds  could be the difference between being  brutally murdered or having a two-on-one  scenario  the best swordsman has no chance against  two warriors  oh there's a story to unearth too  basically after fighting each other for  a thousand years  the vikings samurai and knights are  about to broke a piece  but arrow shooting bad lady apollyon  decides she likes war and wants it to  continue  a perfectly ridiculous storyline for a  perfectly ridiculous game  bravo finally game types in addition to  the campaign we have access to five  different game types to battle through  dominion mode is essentially conquest or  domination in battlefield and has four  players and their minions fight another  four players and their minions  their task is to hold three combat zones  inspirationally titled  a b and c it's also skirmish which is  essentially the same as this but without  the capture points  brawl is a two on two versus mod in  which speed plays a key part  allowing you to team up against one  hapless opponent  duel is a straight-up one-on-one affair  where your defensive skills will be  tested  and finally elimination which is a 4 and  4 death fest  where everyone has a single life so  that's seven reasons to be excited about  for honor  will you be picking this game up and  more importantly who do you think would  win in a fight between knights  samurai and vikings please do me a favor  and massage my ego by pressing that  subscribe  button i'm adam from psg i'll see you  next time
 

